# Managed by unattended-installer.
#
# Format:
#   MODE PRESENCE PROFILE_FILE EXECUTABLE_PROBE
#
# MODE is enforce, complain, or disable.
# PRESENCE is required, optional, or if-executable.
# PROFILE_FILE is relative to /etc/apparmor.d and must not contain slashes.
# EXECUTABLE_PROBE is "-" unless PRESENCE is if-executable.
#
# Repository-owned wrapper, control-plane, and desktop application profiles use
# the managed least-privilege abstractions. Desktop host profiles select enforce
# or complain for this complete set through DESKTOP_APPARMOR_STATE during target
# staging. Wrapper sources default to complain in this tracked template so an
# unrendered desktop policy cannot unexpectedly enforce them. Selected
# package-owned Code and browser profiles follow the same desktop state because
# they use repository-managed local rules. PowerShell remains in complain mode
# because it is an administrative shell intended to execute arbitrary host
# commands. crun and Timeshift use complete repository-owned attachments and
# are enforced independently of the desktop profile state. Tailscale is
# enforced after review of its fresh-install daemon and bootstrap activity.
# Other service, browser, container, and vendor profiles remain in complain mode
# until their workload-specific ALLOWED events have been reviewed.
#
# apparmor-managed-modes reconciles only this declared profile policy. Kernel
# selection, kernel configuration, boot command-line flags, LSM ordering, and
# AppArmor feature availability are preconfigured by the installer and are not
# probed or revalidated by the mode helper.

# Repository-managed desktop wrapper and control-plane source.
complain required managed-desktop-wrappers -

# Repository-managed system, storage, first-boot, Podman, and optional GitLab
# Runner wrapper policy.
complain required managed-system-wrappers -

# Repository-managed status reader used by the privileged security launcher.
complain required usr.sbin.aa-status -

# Repository-managed desktop application profiles.
enforce required whisper-local-transcription -
